--- a/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
+++ b/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
@@ -998,6 +998,20 @@ Below are a few illustrations:
 
   [Try the above config](https://play.victoriametrics.com/select/0/prometheus/graph/#/relabeling?config=-+if%3A+%27%7Bjob%3D%7E%22api-service-.*%22%2Cenv%21%3D%22dev%22%7D%27%0A++source_labels%3A+%5Bjob%5D%0A++target_label%3A+job%0A++replacement%3A+prod_%241&labels=%7B__name__%3D%22http_requests_total%22%2Cjob%3D%22api-service-orders%22%2C+env%3D%22staging%22%2C+instance%3D%2210.0.0.5%3A8080%22%7D)
 
+- Change the case of `job` label values with `action: uppercase` or `action: lowercase`, or strip
+  leading/trailing whitespace from label values (for example, when a value was copied from a source
+  that adds a trailing newline, or assembled by concatenating several `source_labels`) with
+  `action: trim`. These actions accept `source_labels` and `target_label` in the same way as the
+  `replacement`-based rules above, but compute the new `target_label` value automatically instead of
+  requiring a `replacement` template:
+
+  ```yaml
+  metric_relabel_configs:
+    - source_labels: [job]
+      target_label: job
+      action: trim
+  ```
+
